  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There is a problem with the \"[Error:10/15/2017 9:09:48 PM] Room download stalled and timed out, may have lost connection. Resetting.\"\n\nThis happens even when the download is finished but the room is too large to load in time, thus you timeout and can't load the room.\n\nTo clarify: you \"timeout\" on loading the room and not on downloading. \nThis makes you unable to join larger rooms if your computer can't load the room quick enough.\n\nThis is major problem for me as my room is rather large at 400mb~ and takes a while to load, several people complain that they can't enter the room and get kicked back to HUB.\n\nAn easy way to recreate this bug is to stress your CPU with something like baking lightmaps then try to start up VRChat, this leaves you in an infinite loop attempting to load the HUB and timing out.",
